---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How FetchSubs handles data: no accounts, no stored video links or subtitle files. Which analytics and advertising cookies are used and how to opt out."
>
<div class="doc-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>Last updated: November 22, 2026</p>

    <p>
        This policy explains what data is processed when you use fetchsubs.com ("FetchSubs"), operated by Halit Burak Eroğlu
        (<a href="mailto:halitburakeroglu@gmail.com">halitburakeroglu@gmail.com</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>1. What FetchSubs itself collects</h2>
    <p>
        FetchSubs has no user accounts and no sign-up form. When you paste a YouTube link, the server uses it to fetch that video's public caption
        information from YouTube and returns the result to your browser. The link and the subtitle file are processed in memory for that request
        only; they are not written to a database and are not used to build a profile of you.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Server and security logs</h2>
    <p>
        Like most websites, the hosting infrastructure (including Cloudflare, which protects and speeds up the site) records technical request data
        such as IP address, browser type, the page requested, date and time. These logs are used to keep the service running, prevent abuse and fix
        errors, and are kept only as long as needed for those purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Analytics</h2>
    <p>
        FetchSubs uses Google Analytics to understand, in aggregate, how the site is used (for example which pages are visited and whether downloads
        succeed). Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technologies. You can opt out with the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
    <p>
        FetchSubs is free and funded by ads served by Google. Google and its partners use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and
        other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on those visits.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
        <li>You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
        <li>Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for consent before personalized ads and non-essential
        cookies are used, through a consent message managed by Google.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        FetchSubs itself does not need cookies to work. The cookies placed on your device come from the analytics and advertising services described
        above. You can delete or block cookies in your browser settings; the subtitle tool keeps working without them.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Children</h2>
    <p>FetchSubs is a general-audience tool and does not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
        Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR in the EU or KVKK in Türkiye), you may have the right to access, correct or delete
        personal data and to object to its processing. Because FetchSubs does not keep user records, most requests concern the third-party services
        above, which you can manage through the links provided. For anything else, email
        <a href="mailto:halitburakeroglu@gmail.com">halitburakeroglu@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with an updated date at the top.</p>

    <p>See also: <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> · <a href="/contact">Contact</a></p>
</div>

</Layout>
